      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Cotton has long dominated Gates’ economy, thanks to fertile Hatchie River bottomlands that fed West Tennessee’s booming cotton industry.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8,
        28
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/gates_tennessee",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "During World War II, an Army air base opened at nearby Halls in 1942, training B‑17 pilots and boosting local demand for crops.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
